{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"772c747a3826578c2ae2e70e28f5f591adcb9b76bce08df4add16fdb5c040b0a","slug":"free-surface-in-underworld","location":"/articles/free-surface-in-underworld/free-surface-in-underworld.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Free surface in Underworld","banner":"/underworldcode.org-preview/c468a06e88/build/banner-74ecfea4e97e4a147e1f7e1132d408a1.jpg","authors":[{"nameParsed":{"literal":"Neng Lu","given":"Neng","family":"Lu"},"name":"Neng Lu","orcid":"0000-0001-9424-2315","affiliations":["Australian National University"],"id":"contributors-free-surface-in-underworld-generated-uid-0"}],"affiliations":[{"id":"Australian National University","name":"Australian National University"}],"date":"2021-12-03","doi":"10.6084/m9.figshare.33193503","license":{"content":{"id":"CC-BY-4.0","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","name":"Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International","free":true,"CC":true}},"exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"free-surface-in-underworld.md","url":"/underworldcode.org-preview/c468a06e88/build/free-surface-in-unde-dffaa1dcf9aa5c0bc04e1f7b18c641a6.md"},{"format":"typst","filename":"free-surface-in-underworld.pdf","url":"/underworldcode.org-preview/c468a06e88/build/free-surface-in-unde-b5452785654ea5d7d40edd978006b092.pdf"}],"open_access":true,"github":"https://github.com/underworld-technical-notes/underworldcode.org","numbering":{"title":{"offset":2}},"source_url":"https://github.com/underworld-technical-notes/underworldcode.org/blob/main/articles/free-surface-in-underworld/free-surface-in-underworld.md","edit_url":"https://github.com/underworld-technical-notes/underworldcode.org/edit/main/articles/free-surface-in-underworld/free-surface-in-underworld.md","thumbnail":"/underworldcode.org-preview/c468a06e88/build/banner-74ecfea4e97e4a147e1f7e1132d408a1.jpg"},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"div","class":"uwtn-banner","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/underworldcode.org-preview/c468a06e88/build/banner-74ecfea4e97e4a147e1f7e1132d408a1.jpg","key":"Jbdu4Fi9eo","urlSource":"figures/banner.jpg"}],"key":"eqMwxx9Eoy"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":25,"column":1},"end":{"line":25,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Free surface in geodynamics simulations","position":{"start":{"line":25,"column":1},"end":{"line":25,"column":1}},"key":"A057i52Mdg"}],"identifier":"free-surface-in-geodynamics-simulations","label":"Free surface in geodynamics simulations","html_id":"free-surface-in-geodynamics-simulations","implicit":true,"key":"DHZJX2mczL"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":27,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Geodynamic simulations increasingly rely on models with a true free surface to investigate questions of tectonic deformation, mantle convection, and coupling of surface processes and lithosphere dynamics. Historically, most mantle convection simulations have been performed with free-slip boundary conditions at the surface. However, the Earth’s surface is a free surface, which implies that both normal and shear stress should be zero at this interface. Moreover, it has been shown that treating the Earth’s surface as a free surface can have a significant effect on lithospheric and mantle dynamics (Schmeling et al., 2008; Kaus et al., 2010).","position":{"start":{"line":27,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"key":"hRNZvbZAN7"}],"key":"ZGYhBlVaW8"},{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/underworldcode.org-preview/c468a06e88/build/F_Slab_kaus2010-92140430b7b22e04e8af439425815538.png","key":"KMDJYJkAyL","urlSource":"figures/F_Slab_kaus2010.png"}],"enumerator":"1","key":"nGjii4ZoTq"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":32,"column":1},"end":{"line":32,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Free subduction experiment in which a linear viscous slab sinks into a linear viscous mantle (Kaus et al., 2010).","position":{"start":{"line":32,"column":1},"end":{"line":32,"column":1}},"key":"iTFtesX4qv"}],"key":"GJXieHWqJs"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":34,"column":1},"end":{"line":34,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Approaches for treating the free surface","position":{"start":{"line":34,"column":1},"end":{"line":34,"column":1}},"key":"KUYqOTjURE"}],"identifier":"approaches-for-treating-the-free-surface","label":"Approaches for treating the free surface","html_id":"approaches-for-treating-the-free-surface","implicit":true,"key":"nojjLZKdSS"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":36,"column":1},"end":{"line":36,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"There have been several approaches to simulate real free surfaces in geodynamic models:","position":{"start":{"line":36,"column":1},"end":{"line":36,"column":1}},"key":"CzyxDI84aK"}],"key":"ndOiYReRmi"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"(1) Body-fitting method (or conforming mesh based method). This method enables the mesh to conform with the topography, a zero normal stress condition can then naturally be applied on the surface. Such configuration employs either a deforming Lagrangian grid or an Arbitrary Lagrangian-Eulerian (ALE) framework.","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"key":"vvPy2nRHjJ"}],"key":"yjPbL9nxCh"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"(2) Another kind of method employs an Eulerian mesh. The Marker-and-Cell method, level-set functions, or hybrid methods are commonly used here. Free-surface tracking techniques allow for the identification of the cells in the flow grid that contain the interface, which allows a free-surface boundary condition to be applied to the interface cells within the grid.","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"key":"EQ0GknGx54"}],"key":"vhlUGHQRE4"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"(3) “Sticky air” method (for a comprehensive review see Crameri et al. (2012)). In this approximation, there is a low-viscosity, low-density layer in the fluid (termed  ‘air’ or ‘water’) above the free surface. Typically a free-slip boundary condition or the open boundary condition is used above the sticky air layer.","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"key":"tYP5ftLGZD"}],"key":"nvIwvMsc4q"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples in underworld2","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"key":"UNSB5rK5r6"}],"identifier":"examples-in-underworld2","label":"Examples in underworld2","html_id":"examples-in-underworld2","implicit":true,"key":"gOFDcIDVbf"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":46,"column":1},"end":{"line":46,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Both the sticky air and free surface can be easily implemented in Underworld2.  The examples are available by using ","position":{"start":{"line":46,"column":1},"end":{"line":46,"column":1}},"key":"rTXWHLyBmJ"},{"type":"link","url":"https://github.com/underworldcode/UWGeodynamics","position":{"start":{"line":46,"column":1},"end":{"line":46,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"UWGeodynamics","position":{"start":{"line":46,"column":1},"end":{"line":46,"column":1}},"key":"gbYPYl3wE2"}],"urlSource":"https://github.com/underworldcode/UWGeodynamics","error":true,"key":"wGwryp8sGz"},{"type":"text","value":" module:","position":{"start":{"line":46,"column":1},"end":{"line":46,"column":1}},"key":"eghxQlkbg8"}],"key":"HgjdqeUND5"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":48,"column":1},"end":{"line":48,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"(1) “Stick air” method:","position":{"start":{"line":48,"column":1},"end":{"line":48,"column":1}},"key":"UjLxChbKhj"}],"key":"Go324RF1nM"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":50,"column":1},"end":{"line":51,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":50,"column":1},"end":{"line":51,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","url":"https://github.com/underworldcode/UWGeodynamics/blob/development/docs/tutorials/Tutorial%5F10%5FThrust%5FWedges.ipynb","position":{"start":{"line":50,"column":1},"end":{"line":50,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Thrust Wedges","position":{"start":{"line":50,"column":1},"end":{"line":50,"column":1}},"key":"J0bWRB9IVo"}],"urlSource":"https://github.com/underworldcode/UWGeodynamics/blob/development/docs/tutorials/Tutorial%5F10%5FThrust%5FWedges.ipynb","data":{"kind":"file","org":"underworldcode","repo":"UWGeodynamics","reference":"development","file":"docs/tutorials/Tutorial%5F10%5FThrust%5FWedges.ipynb","raw":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/underworldcode/UWGeodynamics/development/docs/tutorials/Tutorial%5F10%5FThrust%5FWedges.ipynb"},"internal":false,"protocol":"github","key":"aCl2QB0LXF"},{"type":"text","value":";","position":{"start":{"line":50,"column":1},"end":{"line":50,"column":1}},"key":"CerdZHptZH"}],"key":"plhwrJ6cIr"}],"key":"sInqta2wPi"}],"key":"DQQD7Qa13W"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":52,"column":1},"end":{"line":53,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"(2) Body-fitting method:","position":{"start":{"line":52,"column":1},"end":{"line":52,"column":1}},"key":"uFswkFQt8e"},{"type":"break","position":{"start":{"line":52,"column":1},"end":{"line":52,"column":1}},"key":"YRPXe9LtJ7"},{"type":"text","value":"Free surface can be turned on using the ","position":{"start":{"line":52,"column":1},"end":{"line":52,"column":1}},"key":"fGBOKTNU3q"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":52,"column":1},"end":{"line":52,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Model.freesurface","position":{"start":{"line":52,"column":1},"end":{"line":52,"column":1}},"key":"SKhhYUFNcE"}],"key":"StjZIfAOHF"},{"type":"text","value":" switch.","position":{"start":{"line":52,"column":1},"end":{"line":52,"column":1}},"key":"mfZ5QIoPOo"}],"key":"N7OAFtdGO3"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","value":"Model.freesurface = True","position":{"start":{"line":55,"column":1},"end":{"line":57,"column":1}},"key":"XCg3GHgszS"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":59,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":59,"column":1},"end":{"line":60,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":59,"column":1},"end":{"line":59,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"link","url":"https://github.com/underworldcode/UWGeodynamics/blob/development/docs/examples/1%5F23%5F01%5FFreeSurface%5FSimple%5FExample.ipynb","position":{"start":{"line":59,"column":1},"end":{"line":59,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Simple example","position":{"start":{"line":59,"column":1},"end":{"line":59,"column":1}},"key":"Fs2A2wWDt3"}],"urlSource":"https://github.com/underworldcode/UWGeodynamics/blob/development/docs/examples/1%5F23%5F01%5FFreeSurface%5FSimple%5FExample.ipynb","data":{"kind":"file","org":"underworldcode","repo":"UWGeodynamics","reference":"development","file":"docs/examples/1%5F23%5F01%5FFreeSurface%5FSimple%5FExample.ipynb","raw":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/underworldcode/UWGeodynamics/development/docs/examples/1%5F23%5F01%5FFreeSurface%5FSimple%5FExample.ipynb"},"internal":false,"protocol":"github","key":"CqtRsZlWxg"},{"type":"text","value":",","position":{"start":{"line":59,"column":1},"end":{"line":59,"column":1}},"key":"KgiiNy079U"}],"key":"GRu9sTx3aX"}],"key":"ZllTt6N6jF"}